|# neutron-windows.ui-radialcontroller-null
|#
|# Premiere project-load CRASH fix (c0000005). Touches: dlls/windows.ui/radialcontroller.c,
|# which is added by wine-tkg's staging patches, so this applies on top of those.
|#
|# RadialController is the Surface Dial API. Wine's IRadialControllerInterop::CreateForWindow
|# called factory_RadialController_ActivateInstance -- which returns E_NOTIMPL WITHOUT writing
|# the out-param -- and then returned S_OK. The caller therefore saw success plus an unwritten
|# (NULL/garbage) pointer, called a method on it, and jumped through a null vtable. Observed as
|# an unhandled c0000005 with rax=rbx=0 when Premiere loads a project.
|#
|# CreateForWindow/GetForWindow are documented FAILABLE APIs -- Surface Dial is optional
|# hardware -- so the correct answer is a clean failure with a NULLed out-param, which makes
|# the app take its no-dial path. Also NULLs the out-param in both ActivateInstance stubs so
|# no other caller can inherit the same garbage.
|--- a/dlls/windows.ui/radialcontroller.c
|+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/radialcontroller.c
--------------------------
