|dwrite: trailing whitespace must not cause a line to wrap.
|
|WHAT THE USER SEES: in Media Encoder and After Effects, UI titles render broken across
|several rows instead of inline -- "Frame Size" appears as "Frame" above "Size". It looks
|like a multi-word problem; it is not. SINGLE words break too ("Format", "Preset",
|"Status"), which is what finally pointed at the real trigger.
|
|ROOT CAUSE: every one of Adobe's labels ends in a TRAILING SPACE. The drawbot measures the
|label with IDWriteTextLayout::GetMetrics().width -- which by specification EXCLUDES trailing
|whitespace -- and then lays the string out at exactly that width. Wine's line breaker counted
|the trailing space toward the line width, so every such label overflowed by exactly the width
|of that space, and DWRITE_WORD_WRAPPING_WRAP rewound to the last break opportunity. That is
|why "Frame Size " became "Frame" / "Size " and "Format " became "Format" + a line holding
|only the space. DirectWrite carries both `width` and `widthIncludingTrailingWhitespace`
|precisely because trailing whitespace must not participate in this decision.
|
|THE FIX: keep accumulating `width` exactly as before and SNAPSHOT it into
|`width_no_trailing_ws` at each non-whitespace cluster; compare that in both overflow tests.
|
|⚠️ IT MUST BE A SNAPSHOT, NOT ARITHMETIC -- two earlier attempts failed on floating point,
|both caught only by the harness:
|  * deferring the additions (`width += trailing_ws + w`) RE-ASSOCIATES the sum -> 3 failures;
|  * subtracting afterwards (`width - trailing_ws`) is inexact, (a+b)-b != a -> 7 failures.
|Both shifted results by an ulp, which made strings whose natural width lands on a
|representable boundary wrap at their own width -- i.e. they reproduced the very bug being
|fixed, in fewer cases. A snapshot is the exact partial sum, bit-identical to what the old
|code compared, so text with NO trailing whitespace is provably unaffected.
|
|EVIDENCE:
|  * Traced from the app itself (`NEUTRON_DWRITE_LAYOUTTRACE=1`, preserved as
|    preserved-fixes/neutron-dwrite-layouttrace-diag.patch), which reported e.g.
|    `LINES layoutW=36.684 textW=36.684 lines=2 text=L"Format "` and
|    `LINES layoutW=55.152 textW=32.400 lines=2 text=L"Frame Size "`.
|  * Regression test preserved-fixes/harnesses/wrapinvariant.c: 17 strings (9 of them the
|    real trailing-space labels lifted verbatim from that trace) x 4 families x 5 sizes x 2
|    weights -> PASS, 0 violations, with the sanity leg (`natW-0.01` must still wrap) still
|    firing 680 times so the test can still fail.
|  * User-confirmed in Media Encoder: column headers render inline.
|
|⚠️ AN EARLIER RUN OF THAT HARNESS REPORTED "0 violations" WHILE BOTH APPS WERE VISIBLY
|BROKEN -- because none of its 8 strings had a trailing space. A harness only disproves what
|it actually exercises. The trailing-space strings are now in it permanently.
|
|This is a DirectWrite conformance bug, not an Adobe quirk: it affects any application that
|measures with `width` and then lays out at that value. Upstream-suitable.
|
|--- a/dlls/dwrite/layout.c
|+++ b/dlls/dwrite/layout.c
--------------------------
